{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/573206-a-thought-i-had-about-changelings-with-very-fantastical-miens-high-wyrd","id":573206,"title":"A thought I had about changelings with very fantastical Miens/high Wyrd.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-29T14:59:42-07:00","id":573206,"title":"A thought I had about changelings with very fantastical Miens/high Wyrd.","content":"Sometimes they don't even have flesh (or at least, no human flesh) anymore. This can happen with any Seeming/Kith combination, but Elementals are very prone to it.<br /> <br /> Despite that, I never saw any indications that these specific changelings stop feeling hungry, thirsty, tired etc. And I can see why. You're no Gentry, you are a hybrid of sorts. I like to think that when these changelings have to eat, they do so in weird or even symbolic ways. An Elemental Ifrit sets his food on fire and absorbs the smoke into his body. The Mask still makes it look like he's using a fork and knife, but people inevitably notice the faint smell of smoke when he eats. They might assume you smoked a cigarette or even weed really quick somehow. Maybe they start looking for any suspicious things in their groceries. If the elemental is lucky, he might hide it as some rare genetic flaw in his salivary glands or something. <br /> <br /> A Darkling Gravewight releases fat flies into his food, which dissolve it, suck it up and then go back into him.<br /> <br /> A Wizened Chirurgeon neatly cuts the food into little pieces, which he stitches into himself. Or maybe he can turn food into a paste which he inserts into his abdomen via a plastic tube like IV treatment.<br /> <br /> The list goes on.<br /> <br /> That's just something I thought was cool, of course, and not every player wants to make up excuses for why this or that weird thing always happens when his PC is around. That's one of the marks of high Wyrd, but there are other marks which the player can describe with more detail.<br /> <br /> Oh, and if you take the idea from Equinox Road that Wyrd 10 changelings turn into Gentry as canon in your game, you could write some neat narrations about how this gnawing, abstract hunger sets in his guts, the most luxurious meals start tasting like cardboard, he keeps eating but he only gets hungrier...and when he goes to get his Glamour fix, he finds that the hunger pangs are gone. They are replaced soon enough with an urge beyond hunger. An urge to go back <b>There.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T05:50:27-07:00","id":573826,"title":"","content":"Well, in my experience, that's the kind of thing that happens at high Wyrd and low Clarity. In general, in any game, the lower your Supernatural Tolerance and higher your Integrity equivalent, the more human you are. And then, when you start gaining power and losing Integrity, you start becoming more fantastical, more of a monster that feeds off that stuff. Especially if we're in the Hedge and can consider it a form of fruit to eat.<br /> <br /> Remember, we're dealing with a sliding scale here, not absolutes. There's a lot of differences here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}